	<description>Originally published in 1965, &lt;i&gt;The Painted Bird&lt;/i&gt; established Jerzy Kosinski as a major literary figure. Called by the Los Angeles Times "one of the most imposing novels of the decade," it was eventually translated into more than thirty languages.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;A harrowing story that follows the wanderings of a boy abandoned by his parents during World War II, &lt;i&gt;The Painted Bird&lt;/i&gt; is a dark story that examines the proximity of terror and savagery to innocence and love. It is the first, and the most famous, novel by a writer who is now discredited.</description>
